    <ol>
      <li><strong>Checkbox</strong> — 18px, 2px corner, 2px border in
          secondary text color; checked = <code>--fl-accent</code> fill with a
          surface-colored check.</li>
      <li><strong>Radio</strong> — 18px circle; checked = accent 2px ring plus
          an accent dot drawn as a radial-gradient (stays themable — no
          hardcoded image color).</li>
      <li><strong>Switch</strong> — 36×20 pill; off = <code>--fl-disabled</code>
          track with surface thumb, on = <code>--fl-tint</code> track with
          accent thumb — the M2 state pair without the thumb shadow.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Classes are the whole API:</strong> <code>fl-check</code>,
        <code>fl-radio</code>, <code>fl-switch</code> go straight on the
        input. There is no required wrapper — pair with a
        <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> (wrapping or <code>for</code>/<code>id</code>)
        so the text toggles the control.</li>
    <li><strong>Switches are checkboxes underneath:</strong> keep
        <code>type="checkbox"</code> and add <code>role="switch"</code> for
        the announcement; the name <code>fl-switch</code> only changes the
        drawing.</li>
    <li><strong>Radios share a <code>name</code></strong> — that is what makes
        them exclusive; wrap the group in <code>fieldset</code>/<code>legend</code>
        (the demos do) rather than a bare <code>div</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Rows:</strong> flex with a 12px gap, control first, 14px text
        label second — same pattern in the demo; the controls are
        <code>flex: 0 0 auto</code> so they never squish.</li>
    <li><strong>Disabled</strong> is the native attribute: boxes/rings gray
        out to <code>--fl-divider</code>, checked glyphs keep their shape in
        <code>--fl-disabled</code>; the switch dims to M2-style 45% emphasis.
        Disabled controls are skipped by tab order.</li>
    <li><strong>Keyboard:</strong> Space toggles checkbox/switch, arrows move
        radio selection — all platform behavior, untested by us because the
        platform guarantees it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every control needs a real text label — icon-only toggles have no
        name; the wrapping-label pattern in the demos is the default.</li>
    <li>Radio groups want a <code>legend</code>; without it, a screen reader
        announces "Team, radio button, 2 of 3" with no idea of what for.</li>
    <li><code>role="switch"</code> on the switch input gives assistive tech
        the right announcement while keeping native toggling.</li>
    <li>State is drawn with fill/ring changes that also follow the global
        <code>:focus-visible</code> ring — never remove that outline.</li>
    <li>Don't disable a checkbox to "explain" something — disabled inputs
        are unfocusable and unannounced; if the user must know why, use
        helper text or a non-interactive note.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
